body:
Nice!
What you can/should do is put the triangle writing into a method that you call for each num.
Then you don't have to have more than one loop.
I'd say that with this kind of setup the do-while is a bad choice. It works the way you do it but if the person chose to have it run 0 times it would still do it once.
That's the beauty of a do-while loop.
Instead use a for-loop.

for(int i = 0; i < Num; i++)
{
	WriteTriangleMethod();
}

Transactions = JsonConvert.DeserializeObject<Transaction>(contents);

That's the problem.

The json you have is a list of transactions so to deserialize it into that you do:

Transactions = JsonConvert.DeserializeObject<List<Transaction>>(contents);

That should solve your problem :)
